data: {"type":"final","report":{"rootCause":"Stripe Payment Intents API degradation at 14:18Z caused checkout-api P99 latency to spike from 280ms to 3200ms; circuit breaker tripped OPEN at 14:22:45Z, converting upstream partial failure into complete checkout outage (100% 503s) due to missing graceful degradation fallback.","recommendations":["IMMEDIATE: Audit stripe_idempotency_key enforcement across all charge.create call sites; if gaps exist, apply emergency fix before enabling async-queue fallback to prevent double-charges on retry","URGENT: Enable async-queue fallback for charge.create with 'payment pending' UX state; surface queue drain status to operations team for manual recovery trigger once Stripe status page shows recovery","SHORT-TERM: Reduce circuit breaker half-open probe interval from 30s to 15s with max 3 retries before re-opening; validate this change in staging against synthetic Stripe failure scenarios before prod deployment","BLOCKING: Validate internal resource saturation (thread pools, connection pools, CPU) within checkout-api during 14:21-14:23Z window—confirm whether internal constraints exacerbated upstream Stripe latency or if 3.2s spike was entirely upstream-driven","ARCHITECTURAL: Implement proactive Stripe status webhook polling (or subscribe to Stripe status change events) to trigger early mitigation (e.g., circuit breaker preemptive half-open transition, queue activation) before P99 spike reaches customers"],"confidence":"high"}}

